{"id": 94, "ts": 1780740344.8995035, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. The additional confirmation from Agent\u202f2 that Candidate\u202fB exhibits clear crew\u2011cooperation problems\u2014being \u201cgrumpy,\u201d \u201cuncooperative,\u201d and making \u201cnasty remarks\u201d about colleagues\u2014reinforces the risk that B could undermine cockpit resource management on long\u2011distance flights. While we still lack direct observations of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s leadership, his 100\u202f% reliability, ability to make quick correct decisions, and the fact that he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew\u201d together indicate a solid foundation for effective crew interaction and implicit leadership in the cockpit. Given that reliability and crew cooperation are non\u2011negotiable, and that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s strengths in these areas are well\u2011documented, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
