{"id": 98, "ts": 1780740380.2076824, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I acknowledge Agent\u202f1\u2019s strong case for Candidate\u202fC, especially the 100\u202f% reliability and calmness in crisis. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the better overall fit.\u202fB is very conscientious and handles stress exceptionally well\u2014critical for the fatigue and pressure of long\u2011distance flights.\u202fHis ability to assess weather conditions accurately and his excellent computer skills directly support the technical and decision\u2011making demands of international routes. While B can be pretentious and occasionally adopts the wrong tone, the documented crew\u2011cooperation problems are limited to tone and attitude, not the fundamental communication breakdowns noted for C (difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, low willingness for further education). Those latter issues raise serious concerns about C\u2019s adaptability, feedback orientation, and sustained crew interaction on extended missions. Given that B\u2019s strengths in reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence outweigh his more modest interpersonal flaws, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
