{"id": 102, "ts": 1780740423.140914, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit. While Agent\u202f3 rightly highlights B\u2019s stress resilience and technical skills, we must weigh the seriousness of the documented crew\u2011cooperation concerns. B \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues,\u201d which directly threatens the collaborative cockpit environment essential for long\u2011distance operations. Moreover, his \u201crelatively weak memory for numbers\u201d raises doubts about his ability to handle critical numerical data under pressure\u2014a core safety requirement. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d and \u201cunderstands complicated technology,\u201d all of which are decisive for safe, high\u2011risk international flights. Although C \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d these issues are less likely to cause immediate safety breakdowns than B\u2019s overtly hostile attitude and potential numeric\u2011memory lapses. Therefore, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
